<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hittite Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hittites, Hittite</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hittite Empire was a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, at its height in the fourteenth and thirteenth centuries BCE. It rivalled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and destroyed the power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a>, and earlier sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. It has its own profile on the site and collapsed around the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> Age.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hittite-empire.jpg" alt="Hittite Empire" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nissrpska · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hittite_kingdoms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
